From 5b0725bdb640e92edf1b78784e4999ad1055b42e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:14:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] macro: the ARM64 JIT records the failing PC like the
 x86-64 one

Run always reported pc 0 on Android because the ARM64 code never wrote
State::fail_pc; the x86-64 code stores the instruction's PC at its start. Two
instructions per macro instruction (a move and a store), a few milliseconds a
second at Mario Kart World's ~1.7 million macro calls a second.

CodeRabbit on #503: macro_turing_jit_arm64.h:482.

